    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0199" n="93" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg93"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Belgian Minister to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Belgium</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-03-06"><hi rendition="#italic">March 6,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor to
                    inform you that I cabled to the government of the Kongo Free State in Brussels a
                    summary of your letter of February 20, 1905, to the Hon. E. Denby, M. C,
                    concerning conditions in the Kongo.</p>
                <p>The King’s secretary-general for the foreign affairs of the Kongo Free State now
                    instructs me to thank you for that expression of your learned opinion on the
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I take great pleasure in doing so at once, and I beg, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Br. Moncheur</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
